## 4. Critical Boundaries & Integration Points

### 4.1 Three-Layer Selection Stack (Phase 4)
```
CandidateSelector (evidence-based probing + cost ranking)
    ↓ ranked candidates
AdvancedModelSelector (VRAM tier + HPO space)
    ↓ model_sel dict
JITEncoderSelector (final VRAM dry-run on actual GPU)
    ↓ JITResult (encoder names, peak_memory_mb)
Phase 5 training loop
```

> **Boundary:** `CandidateSelector` uses probe accuracy to rank. `JITEncoderSelector` is purely a hardware filter — it does NOT re-rank, only validates the top selection fits VRAM.

### 4.2 XAI Two-Layer Architecture
| Layer | Class | When | Method |
|---|---|---|---|
| Training-time | `XAIExplainer` (via `generate_xai_artifacts`) | Post-best-trial, Phase 5 | Variance proxy (tabular), GradCAM (image), attention weights (text), fusion weights |  
| Post-training (on demand) | `XAIEngine` | `/explain` API call | SHAP DeepExplainer (tabular), attention (text), GradCAM placeholder (image) |

